    <record id="source_cpp_2027_rate_cut" model="l10n_ca.payroll.source">
        <field name="sequence">80</field>
        <field name="jurisdiction">federal</field>
        <field name="kind">statute</field>
        <field
            name="name"
        >Spring Economic Update 2026 Implementation Act, S.C. 2026, c. 22</field>
        <field name="publisher">Department of Finance Canada</field>
        <field name="reference">Bill C-30, Division 5 (CPP base rate)</field>
        <field
            name="url"
        >https://www.canada.ca/en/department-finance/news/2026/06/legislation-passes-to-implement-measures-from-the-spring-economic-update-2026.html</field>
        <field
            name="summary"
        >Base CPP rate from 9.9% to 9.5% (employee and employer combined): the 2027 versions of the CPP rates, which the CRA applies from January 1, 2027.</field>
        <field name="state">to_verify</field>
        <field
            name="verification_note"
        >Division 5 (s. 41 to 44) comes into force on a day fixed by order in council under s. 114(4) of the Canada Pension Plan, which needs the consent of two thirds of the included provinces having two thirds of their population (s. 44(2) of the Act). No such order appears in the Canada Gazette, Part II, up to the issue of November 4, 2026, and the CPP consolidation lists s. 41 to 43 as not in force; the CRA already publishes 5.75% for 2027. Check the Canada Gazette, Part II, for the order, and https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/AnnualStatutes/2026_22/FullText.html.</field>
    </record>
